  "result": "The gate still returns **WITNESS_FAIL**, and the cause is the node's planned `blind` scenario, not the rule. I stopped after 3 of 6 runs and reported it as a node defect in `task_result.md`.\n\n**The rule** is written as the record states it, with no narrowings:\n- **Subject class:** the subject must be a `DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle`.\n- **Applicability:** `.tt`, because the record's applicability is just that subject class, which the binder already carries.\n- **Obligation:** for every road user `m` that is not the subject, is a motorcycle or moped, and occupies a highway, and every lane `L` that `m` occupies: the subject must not occupy `L` while `rel_longitudinal_overlap(subject, m) ≥ 0`.\n\n**Witnesses:** these pass:\n- **Planned:** `forbid`, `permit`, `idle`, `branch_1`, `branch_2`.\n- **Added:** `branch_3`, which uses a moped (violated), and `branch_4`, where the motorcycle is on no highway (compliant). They make sure the moped and highway parts of the rule are tested.\n\n**Why `blind` fails:** it can't be built so that it reports unknown.\n- Masking `rel.longitudinal_overlap` only removes a supplied (measured) value. Core then works the overlap out from position, heading and body size.\n- Core requires those same three fields for any road user whose lane occupancy is observed, and the narrative needs both vehicles' occupancy observed.\n- So the overlap is always computed and the scene comes out violated (run 1).\n- I tried removing the motorcycle's body size; Core refused the trace (run 2). I then also made its occupancy unobserved; the result was unknown, but because of occupancy rather than the masked atom, which the gate rejects (run 3).\n- I put `blind` back to the scene as planned so the files show the defect plainly.\n\n**What the plan needs to change:** `blind`'s masked list, either:\n- add `kin.extent` next to `rel.longitudinal_overlap`, which the node would need to allow, or\n- mask `rel.occupies` instead, with a narrative like \"car beside the motorcycle; lane occupancy not observed.\"\n\nFiles are in `.../results/full221-1116-1018/iter-002/code/NRS_486_341/`:\n- task_result.md",
